A wildcard mask is basically the opposite of a subnet mask.
In OSPF, it's used to tell OSPF which interface IP addresses to match.
Comparison
Subnet Mask	Wildcard Mask
255.255.255.0	0.0.0.255
255.255.0.0	0.0.255.255
255.0.0.0	0.255.255.255

What does it mean?
In a wildcard mask:
0 = must match exactly
255 = can be anything
Example:
network 10.1.1.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
means:
10.1.1.X
where X can be any value from 0 to 255.
So these interfaces match:
10.1.1.1
10.1.1.10
10.1.1.254
but these do not:
10.1.2.1
10.2.1.1


